<Defs>

  <!--
    The Circuit of Tamers (docs/design/peoples-next.md, the third of the eight; docs/design/peoples.md, "Release D";
    Source/ColonyCouncil/Peoples/PeoplesD.cs): beast-tamers who walk the region with their companions, challenging every
    keeper of beasts they meet to a friendly bout; with PokéWorld their companions are Pokémon, without it the region's
    beasts (and Vanilla Animals Expanded's where it has put them on the land). Industrial, on the game's outlander parent;
    they arise in every age (ariseAges 0~3): in the tribal and medieval ages their rangers carry bows (ageArms), in the
    spacer age a few are Wildspeakers (Vanilla Psycasts Expanded; PeopleGift.ages). Travelling clothes, freely varied,
    around their signature: a braided sash in the Circuit's violet with a token for every bout won (Biotech's sash, and
    its bandolier where one is worn). Their towns keep bout-rings, a hatchery and stables for every kind
    (Rimfolk_Plan_BoutRing). At the gate: a tamer challenges the colony's best trainer to a friendly bout by the
    Fighting-type spar's rules, a bruise one bout in 25 through the harm setting's budget (Rimfolk_Evt_TamerBout); an
    egg-trader offers an egg of the Circuit's hatchery, swapped or sold (Rimfolk_Evt_EggTrade); a ranger brings home one
    of the colony's animals that strayed (Rimfolk_Evt_TamerStray). Their ask: a young beast raised for their stables
    (Rimfolk_Mission_TamersFoal). Their founding: Nessa Pell, the herder girl who found an egg in a meteor crater and
    walked the region with what hatched for forty years. Original names only: nothing is borrowed from any game's trainer
    ranks. Faith (Ideology): animals are people (animal personhood), each tamer their own champion (individualist), and
    the road (VE Memes' nomad); the animalist style. Kinds of people: Alpha Genes' animusen, saurids, yttakin, VRE's
    animakin, Venators and wood elves, three in four baseliners.
  -->

  <FactionDef ParentName="OutlanderFactionBase">
    <defName>Rimfolk_Tamers</defName>
    <label>circuit of tamers</label>
    <description>Beast-tamers who walk the region with their companions and challenge every keeper of beasts they meet to a friendly bout. A tamer travels with one or two beasts that would follow them anywhere, and the Circuit's highest honour is to be beaten fairly by a stranger. Their towns keep bout-rings, a hatchery and stables for every kind.\n\nTheir ways began with a herder girl called Nessa Pell, who found an egg in the crater a falling star had made and raised what hatched from it. She walked the region with it for forty years, challenging every keeper of beasts she met, and the Circuit grew from those she beat and those who beat her. A tamer still wears a braided sash with a token tied on for every bout won, and Pell's own sash, they say, hangs in the oldest ring with no room left on it.\n\nThey are cheerful, competitive and generous in defeat, and they speak of their beasts as friends, never as property. A bond is not a leash, they say, and they mean it. Each ring is kept by its ring-keeper, and the Circuit by its circuit-holder.</description>
    <pawnSingular>tamer</pawnSingular>
    <pawnsPlural>tamers</pawnsPlural>
    <leaderTitle>circuit-holder</leaderTitle>
    <techLevel>Industrial</techLevel>
    <basicMemberKind>Rimfolk_Tamers_Tamer</basicMemberKind>
    <factionNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_Tamers</factionNameMaker>
    <settlementNameMaker>Rimfolk_Namer_TamersTown</settlementNameMaker>
    <factionIconPath>ColonyCouncil/Peoples/Tamers</factionIconPath>
    <settlementTexturePath>ColonyCouncil/Peoples/TamersTown</settlementTexturePath>
    <colorSpectrum>
      <li>(0.40, 0.24, 0.58)</li>
      <li>(0.58, 0.40, 0.76)</li>
    </colorSpectrum>
    <hidden>false</hidden>
    <naturalEnemy>false</naturalEnemy>
    <permanentEnemy>false</permanentEnemy>
    <canSiege>false</canSiege>
    <requiredCountAtGameStart>0</requiredCountAtGameStart>
    <startingCountAtWorldCreation>1</startingCountAtWorldCreation>
    <maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>9999</maxConfigurableAtWorldCreation>
    <configurationListOrderPriority>18</configurationListOrderPriority>
    <settlementGenerationWeight>0.5</settlementGenerationWeight>
    <raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve Inherit="False">
      <points>
        <li>(0, 0.25)</li>
      </points>
    </raidCommonalityFromPointsCurve>
    <xenotypeSet Inherit="False">
      <xenotypeChances>
        <Yttakin MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.03</Yttakin>
        <Hussar MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.02</Hussar>
        <Highmate MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.02</Highmate>
        <Pigskin MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech">0.02</Pigskin>
        <AG_Animusen MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,sarg.alphagenes">0.04</AG_Animusen>
        <VRESaurids_Saurid MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,vanillaracesexpanded.saurid">0.02</VRESaurids_Saurid>
        <VRE_Animakin MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,Ludeon.RimWorld.Royalty,vanillaracesexpanded.phytokin">0.02</VRE_Animakin>
        <DV_Venator MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,det.venators">0.02</DV_Venator>
        <DevDesigner_XenotypeWoodElves MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech,DevDesigner.Elves.Continued">0.02</DevDesigner_XenotypeWoodElves>
      </xenotypeChances>
    </xenotypeSet>
    <fixedIdeo>true</fixedIdeo>
    <ideoName>The Freely Given Bond</ideoName>
    <ideoDescription>A bond is not a leash. A beast is a person of its own kind, owed its keep, its say and its friendship, and a tamer wins its trust or nothing at all; what is won is won together. Each tamer is their own champion and walks their own circuit, and the highest honour there is comes from a stranger who beats them fairly. Nessa Pell walked the region for forty years with what hatched from a star's egg, and the Circuit walks it still.</ideoDescription>
    <forcedMemes>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">AnimalPersonhood</li>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">Individualist</li>
      <!-- Pell's forty years on the road: Vanilla Ideology Expanded's nomad. -->
      <li MayRequire="VanillaExpanded.VMemesE">VME_Nomad</li>
    </forcedMemes>
    <structureMemeWeights Inherit="False">
