          <li>Muffalo</li>
          <li>Alpaca</li>
          <li>Husky</li>
          <li>Chicken</li>
        </herd>
        <herdCount>8~14</herdCount>
        <ariseAges>0~3</ariseAges>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </FactionDef>

  <!-- ===================== Their people ===================== -->

  <!--
    How alike they look (docs/design/peoples.md, "Release D"): travelling clothes of every make, freely varied (the
    game's and Vanilla Apparel Expanded's shirts, jackets and hats, Settlers' bandanas and vests, packs), around the
    Circuit's sash in violet (Biotech's sash, and its bandolier where one is worn), a token on it for every bout won.
    The ring-wardens who keep order at the bout-rings are their only guards, and share one kit: a jacket, a helmet and
    the sash. Light weapons: revolvers, pistols and knives; rifles for the rangers. Each tamer is good with beasts, and a
    few are A RimWorld of Magic's druids, summoners or rangers; in the spacer age a few are Wildspeakers (Vanilla
    Psycasts Expanded). In the tribal and medieval ages their rangers carry bows. They carry kibble, hay or herbs for
    their beasts. Without any mod: the game's shirts, trousers, jackets, dusters and hats, revolvers and knives.
  -->
  <PawnKindDef Name="Rimfolk_TamersKindBase" Abstract="True">
    <race>Human</race>
    <defaultFactionDef>Rimfolk_Tamers</defaultFactionDef>
    <chemicalAddictionChance>0.04</chemicalAddictionChance>
    <backstoryCryptosleepCommonality>0.01</backstoryCryptosleepCommonality>
    <invNutrition>2.55</invNutrition>
    <specificApparelRequirements>
      <!-- The Circuit's violet on the sash, and on a bandolier where one is worn. -->
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech"><apparelDef>Apparel_Sash</apparelDef><color>(0.50, 0.32, 0.68)</color></li>
      <li MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Biotech"><apparelDef>Apparel_Bandolier</apparelDef><color>(0.50, 0.32, 0.68)</color></li>
    </specificApparelRequirements>
  </PawnKindDef>

